  "summary": "The previous critiques correctly identify the root cause (on_restart callback not wired in tui.py line 2086) and the sync/async mismatch, but the proposed fix needs sharper scoping. The 'restart TUI' button should mean 'restart the TUI process itself' (os.execv or app.exit with auto-relaunch), not 'restart a pipeline for some feature' — action_restart() is the wrong target because it requires a selected_feature and restarts a pipeline phase, not the TUI. A new async _handle_remote_restart method should be added that (1) cancels any running agents by setting kill_requested on both _plan_agent_status and _implement_agent_status, (2) calls app.exit() or os.execv(sys.executable, ...) to cleanly restart the entire TUI process, and (3) is passed as on_restart=self._handle_remote_restart in the ServerClient instantiation at line 2086. For the modal conversion, both client.html (line 632-648) and index.html (line 1085-1099) should replace confirm()/alert() with the existing .modal-overlay pattern already used for idea creation and move confirmations — but note that the two templates have diverged (index.html uses showToast for success, client.html uses alert), so the modal implementation should standardize both to use the modal for confirmation and showToast for the success/error result. The race condition concern from the previous round is valid but largely moot if restart means 'restart the whole TUI process' rather than 'start a new pipeline run' — killing the process inherently cancels everything."
